        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Why Use This Tool?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Real-time counting:</strong> Numbers update as you type, with
                no button to click.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Multiple metrics at once:</strong> Words, characters, characters
                without spaces, sentences, paragraphs, and reading time in one view.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Limit checker:</strong> See at a glance how many characters
                you have left for an X post, an Instagram caption, a LinkedIn post,
                or a meta description.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Privacy first:</strong> Everything runs in your browser. No
                uploads, no tracking of your text.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Free with no limits:</strong> Count as many texts as you want,
                as often as you want.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Works on any device:</strong> Desktop, laptop, tablet, or
                phone, with no app needed.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Common Use Cases</h3>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">1. Checking Essay Word Limits</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Most academic essays have a word limit, such as 500, 1,000, or 1,500
            words. Paste your draft here and see exactly where you stand. Check
            whether your limit includes headings, footnotes, and the reference
            list, since this tool counts everything you paste.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">2. Planning Blog Posts</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            There is no ideal word count for SEO. What ranks depends on the
            topic and what searchers want. In-depth guides are often 1,000 to
            2,000 words, but a short answer can rank too. Use the count to check
            that your post covers the topic fully, rather than to hit a number.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            3. Staying Within Social Media Limits
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            A standard X (Twitter) post is limited to 280 characters, an
            Instagram caption to 2,200 characters, and a LinkedIn post to 3,000
            characters. Paste your caption here to avoid the "too long" warning.
            Platforms count links and emoji in their own ways, so confirm in the
            app when you are close to the limit.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">4. Writing Meta Descriptions</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Google may cut long meta descriptions short in search results,
            roughly after 150 to 160 characters on desktop, depending on the
            width of the letters, and it sometimes rewrites them. Paste your
            draft here and check the character count before adding it to your
            page's <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            5. Preparing Product Descriptions
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            E-commerce platforms set their own character limits for product
            titles and descriptions, and the limits differ from one platform to
            another. Paste your text here to check it against the limit your
            platform shows.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            6. Checking Reading Time for Articles
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Reading time estimates help set expectations for readers. At {
                READING_WPM
            } words per minute, a 1,000-word article takes about {
                formatDuration(1000, READING_WPM)
            } to read. This tool shows that automatically.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">A Worked Example</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Here's what the tool shows when you paste this paragraph:
        </p>
        <pre
            class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-lg text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4 whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{SAMPLE}</code></pre>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Words:</strong> {sample.words}</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Characters:</strong>
                {sample.chars} (including spaces)
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Characters (no spaces):</strong>
                {sample.noSpaces}
            </li>
            <li><strong>Sentences:</strong> {sample.sentences}</li>
            <li><strong>Paragraphs:</strong> {sample.paragraphs}</li>
            <li><strong>Reading time:</strong> {sample.reading}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 mb-4">
            That's the information you need without opening Word, Google Docs,
            or any other app.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            How Reading Time Is Calculated
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This tool divides your word count by <strong
                >{READING_WPM} words per minute</strong
            >. Studies put the average adult closer to 240 words per minute for
            non-fiction, and popular reading-time calculators use figures from
            about 200 to 265, so {READING_WPM} is a cautious estimate. Technical or
            academic text can take longer than the estimate, and easy fiction often
            reads faster.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Frequently Asked Questions
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
            {
                faqs.map((f) => (
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{f.q}</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">{f.a}</p>
                    </div>
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Tools & Guides -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Tools</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
            <a
                href="/tools/json-formatter/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">JSON Formatter</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Format and validate JSON data.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/qr-generator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">QR Code Generator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Create custom QR codes for any URL.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/password-generator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Password Generator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Create strong, random passwords.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Guides</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
            <a
                href="/blog/how-to-count-words/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">How to Count Words Accurately</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Complete guide for essays, blogs, and social media.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/word-count-google-docs-all-tabs/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">
                    How to Count Words Across All Tabs in Google Docs
                </h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Get the total word count across multiple tabs.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/blog/twitter-character-count/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-medium">Twitter/X Character Count Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Stay within the 280-character limit.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <script>
        interface Limit {
            name: string;
            limit: number;
        }

        const cfg = document.getElementById("calc-config")!;
        const LIMITS: Limit[] = JSON.parse(cfg.dataset.limits!);
        const READING_WPM = Number(cfg.dataset.wpm);

        const input = document.getElementById(
            "text-input",
        ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
        const wordCount = document.getElementById("word-count")!;
        const charCount = document.getElementById("char-count")!;
        const charNoSpaceCount = document.getElementById("char-nospace-count")!;
        const sentenceCount = document.getElementById("sentence-count")!;
        const paragraphCount = document.getElementById("paragraph-count")!;
        const readingTime = document.getElementById("reading-time")!;
        const copyBtn = document.getElementById("copy-btn")!;
        const clearBtn = document.getElementById("clear-btn")!;
        const chips = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".limit-chip");

        const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString("en-US");

        // --- same counting logic as the page frontmatter ---
        function countWords(text: string): number {
            const t = text.trim();
            return t ? t.split(/\s+/).length : 0;
        }

        function countChars(text: string): number {
            if (!text) return 0;
            const Segmenter = (Intl as any).Segmenter;
            if (text.length < 200000 && Segmenter) {
                let n = 0;
                for (const _ of new Segmenter().segment(text)) n++;
                return n;
            }
            return Array.from(text).length;
        }

        function countSentences(text: string): number {
            const t = text.trim();
            if (!t) return 0;
            const ends = t.match(/[.!?]+["')\]]*(?=\s|$)/g);
            const count = ends ? ends.length : 0;
            return /[.!?]["')\]]*$/.test(t) ? count : count + 1;
        }

        function countParagraphs(text: string): number {
            return text.split(/\r?\n/).filter((l) => l.trim() !== "").length;
        }

        function formatDuration(words: number, wpm: number): string {
            if (words === 0) return "0 sec";
            const total = Math.max(1, Math.round((words / wpm) * 60));
            if (total < 60) return `${total} sec`;
            const m = Math.floor(total / 60);
            const s = total % 60;
            return s === 0 ? `${m} min` : `${m} min ${s} sec`;
        }

        function updateLimits(chars: number) {
            chips.forEach((chip) => {
                const limit = Number(chip.dataset.limit);
                const status = chip.querySelector(".limit-status")!;
                const base = "limit-chip px-3 py-1 rounded-full ";
                if (chars === 0) {
                    chip.className = base + "bg-gray-100 text-gray-700";
                    status.textContent = `${fmt(limit)} left`;
                } else if (chars <= limit) {
                    chip.className = base + "bg-green-50 text-green-800";
                    status.textContent = `${fmt(limit - chars)} left`;
                } else {
                    chip.className = base + "bg-red-50 text-red-700";
                    status.textContent = `${fmt(chars - limit)} over`;
                }
            });
        }

        function updateCounts() {
            const text = input.value;
            const words = countWords(text);
            const chars = countChars(text);

            wordCount.textContent = fmt(words);
            charCount.textContent = fmt(chars);
            charNoSpaceCount.textContent = fmt(
                countChars(text.replace(/\s/g, "")),
            );
            sentenceCount.textContent = fmt(countSentences(text));
            paragraphCount.textContent = fmt(countParagraphs(text));
            readingTime.textContent = formatDuration(words, READING_WPM);
            updateLimits(chars);
        }

        input.addEventListener("input", updateCounts);

        let copyTimer: number | undefined;
        copyBtn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
            if (!input.value) return;
            let ok = true;
            try {
                await navigator.clipboard.writeText(input.value);
            } catch {
                try {
                    input.select();
                    ok = document.execCommand("copy");
                } catch {
                    ok = false;
                }
            }
            copyBtn.textContent = ok ? "Copied!" : "Copy failed";
            window.clearTimeout(copyTimer);
            copyTimer = window.setTimeout(
                () => (copyBtn.textContent = "Copy Text"),
                1500,
            );
        });

        clearBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            input.value = "";
            updateCounts();
            input.focus();
        });

        // Count any text the browser restored into the box on load
        updateCounts();
    </script>

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify(webAppSchema)}
    />
    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)}
    />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
</Layout>
